From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] skcms: use _mm256_cvtph_ps instead of a builtin clang 22
 removed

  Transform_inl.h:170:12: error: use of undeclared identifier
  '__builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256'; did you mean '__builtin_ia32_cvtpd2ps256'?

We now build Chromium with the system clang (22) so that it matches the
system libc++ it is compiled against, and clang removed
__builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256. The documented intrinsic _mm256_cvtph_ps does the
same F16C half-to-float conversion, and skcms.cc already includes
<immintrin.h>, so nothing else is needed. This mirrors the USING_AVX512F
branch just above, which already spells it as _mm512_cvtph_ps.

Only this one builtin is affected. The others skcms uses -
__builtin_ia32_vcvtps2ph256 (the reverse conversion), roundps256 and the
gather builtins - were all verified to still compile with clang 22, so they
are deliberately left alone.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h
+++ b/src/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h
@@ -166,8 +166,7 @@
 #elif defined(USING_AVX512F)
     return (F)_mm512_cvtph_ps((__m256i)half);
 #elif defined(USING_AVX_F16C)
-    typedef int16_t __attribute__((vector_size(16))) I16;
-    return __builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256((I16)half);
+    return (F)_mm256_cvtph_ps((__m128i)half);
 #else
     U32 wide = cast<U32>(half);
     // A half is 1-5-10 sign-exponent-mantissa, with 15 exponent bias.
